{
 "case": "N27-C01-NEG",
 "says": "The repository keeps a repository-authored source at its first revision, and the Team platform has installed a published package source at the publisher's revision. Three requests must each be refused by the owner, with nothing written: registering a second, managed home for the repository source (source_home_conflict: one source keeps one home); committing a revision of the installed package whose member bytes differ from the publisher's (publisher_bytes_modified: an addition is a derived source of its own, never an edit in place); and bob, who holds no grant from the Team, asking for a projection of the Team's package source (source_not_authorized). Unrelated and unaccepted state must be untouched afterwards: the repository source's next revision still commits on the head its first revision left, and resolving the package's member still returns the publisher's revision beside the package's one home.",
